# Verification — prd/04-ringmaster.md (turn 18)

## Overall assessment

The file is a complete, well-disciplined Ringmaster PRD that directly answers the developer prompt's Products requirement: it compares the three packaging alternatives (in-process/FFI, separate Rust worker, extension-plus-controller) on native-surface fidelity and failure containment, and recommends the separate supervised Rust worker as an evidence-conditional hypothesis with explicit flip conditions rather than presuming it. Epistemic tagging is thorough — every substantive paragraph and table row carries exactly one of extracted/inferred/proposed/uncertain — and the cited contract, decision, and integration references spot-check clean against the prior accepted files. Accept as-is; there are no downstream dependents.

## Protocol compliance

The raw deliverable (`runs/turn8-20/deliverables/turn18.md`) wraps the content in a single fenced block annotated `markdown:prd/04-ringmaster.md` with no content outside the fence except `<!-- TURN_END:18 -->`, matching the manifest item number. The tree file strips fence and marker correctly and ends at a coherent boundary (§9 plus two closing synthesis sentences). No truncation.

## Structure and scope

Nine sections (purpose/boundary, packaging decision with alternatives and responsibility sketch, native binding and sessions, learn-run-verify-heal execution with tiered resolution and DOM reduction, connector/lifecycle verb table, evidence/safety/learning, acceptance and silo gate with native-access experiment, delivery slices, open decisions) give a sibling-symmetric counterpart to `prd/03-circus-tent.md` at the same depth. The file stays on Ringmaster throughout: it distinguishes Ringmaster from Circus Tent internals, the crawler, job-hunter commissioning, and Hellscape practice, and correctly refuses to invent a native HTTP/RPC service, shared `ElementHandle`, or cross-browser driver.

