## Cross-file consistency

Contract baseline correctly states six `0.1.0` shared contracts (version verified in the contract files). The file preserves the no-shared-implementation boundary (Rust re-implementation of learn-run-heal tiers, no import of Circus Tent Python machinery, providers, cache formats, quotas, or tab-count constants), the connector-declares/consumer-assesses rule, per-subject capability non-inheritance, and the P-14 human-controlled production policy with practice-success-never-flips language. No handoff amendment is introduced, stated explicitly in the decision baseline — amendment discipline satisfied.

